    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (78.49) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.59), who represent our highest-ceiling plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a dynamic platoon advantage (R) and a premium spot in the order, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** exploits the favorable matchup against Brandon Young; his 0.371 xwOBA suggests he is primed to capitalize on a sub-5.00 xERA starter. Close behind, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.89) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.04) provide substantial upside. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is slotted lower in the lineup, his SP matchup against Merrill Kelly\u2014a pitcher we are targeting\u2014combined with the platoon advantage makes him a high-efficiency start, while **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite cornerstone regardless of daily volatility.\n\nOur most critical selection is **Nasim Nunez** (63.18), whose viability is tied directly to the \"scarcity premium.\" While his raw projection is modest, his utility in the SB category is bolstered by the slow delivery of Merrill Kelly, granting him an edge in our efficiency model. The hardest bench decision involved **Josh Jung** (46.89); despite a respectable score, he fell short of the 50.0 threshold required to displace our core, largely due to the difficulty of his matchup against Parker Messick. We are monitoring lineup confirmations closely for **Brayan Rocchio**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Miguel Andujar**, as \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces variance that could force a pivot to the bench if these players drop in the batting order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Miguel Andujar**, whose sub-41 score makes him a risky play; if the official lineup drops him lower than 7th, he will be pulled to preserve our limited game caps.",
